---
description: Alembic migration discipline
globs: migrations/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Never modify an already-applied migration (`0001` and later once applied). Add a new
  revision with `alembic revision`.
- Migrations are hand-written, explicit, and include constraints and downgrade steps.
- Do not weaken or drop safety constraints (CHECKs, UNIQUEs, triggers) without an ADR and
  explicit owner approval.
- Test: `alembic upgrade head`, then `alembic downgrade -1` and `upgrade head` on a scratch
  database only, never on data you care about.
